tips on managing school life  and a business i got a great question  from one of my youtube viewers love you  guys  aftermath who wrote in to say hello evan  i'm only 15 years old and i have started  my own media company events and  marketing  do you have any tips on how to balance  my school life and business  at the same time so it's a great  question and  i was a student entrepreneur you're  starting younger than me i started  really when i was in university  and it can be hard you know it can be  hard when you're trying to balance  running the business with all your  school load plus family obligations and  all that  and it can often seem i remember being  so frustrated especially when exam time  came around  and you know i really wanted to work on  my business and felt like there was just  too much happening in my life  so here are some tips okay here are some  tips for how you can manage  your school life and your business at  the same time number one  is do something every day do something  every single day for your business and  this this applies to anybody if you're  if you're starting a business if you're  doing it part-time you have you know a  full-time job you're starting on the  side  you have other commitments every day you  need to do something to grow your  business  even if you're you know you have an exam  the next day and you're cramming and  you're studying for it you still have to  find  20 minutes to do something for your  business it could be answering emails it  could be reaching out to somebody  whatever it is momentum has to keep  going  you cannot afford to take three weeks  off  and then just come back to the business  you lose too much in that process so  every day no matter how small do  something to grow your business  okay number two is get help  get people to help you out so i was  fortunate i had two business partners  in my business so when things got really  crazy at school  i still had my partners helping me out  but i also hired  people and the first guy i hired was for  one hour a day just an hour a day  doesn't cost a ton of money just to help  do some of the things that i didn't want  to do  anymore you know admin stuff that i  didn't want to take care of  so get some people to help you and this  is something you have to figure out as  you grow  right now you may just be a one-person  shop but you want to get your business  to the point where  you are not required in the day-to-day  running of your company  so it's great practice now to get  started to hire somebody  even for an hour a day you could be  somebody local or go to websites like  odesk.com which i'm a big fan of  and find people to help you out so it's  not just on you all the time  and then number three is incorporate  your school projects into your business  so one of my favorite things to do when  i was in university  i didn't realize this until my last year  was for the elective  projects that you take on  i always try to make it about my  business so  if i had a marketing class and we had to  do a marketing proposal  right or think of a new marketing idea i  would always bring  my company and say okay well here's a  project here's a company  here's a new business that's starting  let's do a marketing plan for this  business  whatever school project i had i always  tried to bring in  my company to be the topic you can't  always do it you know if you're doing a  project on ancient history  you're talking about egyptian times you  may not be able to incorporate your  business into that  but as much as possible and one thing  that i really love doing that really  helped my business out which i only  discovered at the end  i could create my own course and so in  university there's this option  and i don't know if there's an option in  your in your high school or not i  could make an elective course with the  professor as long as the professor said  i will mentor  this entrepreneur then you can create  your own course and so there's no exam  for it  uh you have to basically depends on what  you decide with your professor  but i was able to create a course around  building my business  and have a professor mentor me at the  same time so it provided a lot of great  things for me first of all it meant one  last class i had to study for  at school second of all i got guidance  from  the professor who was helping me out and  third of all i can use the school's  resources so my software actually sold  into universities  and i could go to the scientists at the  universities who would be my customers  and start talking to them about what i  was doing in my company and the  projects we're working on they're  talking to me because i'm a student at  the school of work on this school  project where they wouldn't talk to me  if it was from  this company and so i would investigate  i didn't  that that option wasn't promoted  anywhere i learned about it through a  friend who had done something similar  i don't know there's that option at your  high school but there may be an option  to work with one  professor or teacher i guess there and  create your own course around  your business somehow where they're  mentoring you and they give you a grade  at the end  so definitely investigate that option so  those are things that really helped me  so again just quick recap  do something every day get help and then  incorporate your classes into your  business as much as possible  that's my advice good luck i know it's  hard but keep working every day grinding  out  and believe those are watching like the  video give it a thumbs up below and let  me know what you think leave a comment  underneath you have a question  leave it below make your video response  just like i did for this one  and click on my face to subscribe to the  channel thank you so much and i'll see  you soon
 

